 "notes": [
  "P0 animatic v3 (MP4 review + OGV runtime + poster) verified against checkpoint 16 SHAs (outputs v3 manifest); 5 panels revised in total (4 in checkpoint 13: CIN_001_S03, CIN_001_S06, CIN_004_S01, CIN_004_S03; 1 in checkpoint 16: CIN_002_S02), 7 panels byte-identical to v1; poster unchanged (CIN_001_S01). Separate 16:9 keyframes per shot in Art_Source/Cinematics/P0_Animatic/keyframes_16x9/ (P0_keyframes_16x9_manifest_v1.json).",
  "Timing JSON + SRT per scene copied from Narrative/Deliveries with sha256 verification against the checkpoint 01/05/06 manifests. SRT is UTF-8/NFC, DRAFT.",
  "dialogueCues is derived from parsed timing JSON shots[].dialogue, cross-checked against the parsed SRT cue count and, where present, the source manifest 'cues' list (Gói 30 item 1 / PR119 review finding 1). P0 + CIN_006 source manifests carry no 'cues' key; their counts come from timing/SRT. Any disagreement aborts this build.",
  "Only CIN_001_S05 (24.8-28.5 s, version B) is DECIDED; all other dialogue windows remain PROPOSED_ANIMATIC_PLACEMENT until director/Codex confirms them.",
  "No final picture: animatic is storyboard level (revision v3 fixes all 5 recorded panel defects, not final picture); character keyframes still await lock for locked shots.",
  "Per-scene clips (checkpoint 18, Goi 30 item 6): CIN_001 (36 s), CIN_002 (18 s) and CIN_004 (18 s) each exported as its own MP4 + OGV + poster + SRT + timing + hash manifest under assets/cinematics/<SCENE>/. The 72 s reel stays review/gallery only, NOT auto-run as opening.",
  "CIN_005 animated take (checkpoint 21, Goi 30 item 7): first campaign video with real motion -- 18 s / 3 shots, slow Ken Burns camera moves on 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_005/keyframes_16x9/, CIN005_keyframes_manifest_v1.json). Animatic-level motion, NOT a final pose-animated take; no audio track in the clip (VO/music/ambience added separately in editing); no baked subtitles. Known defect: S02 roof palette drifts from S01.",
  "CIN_006 animated take (checkpoint 22, Goi 30 item 7): the scene leaves PENDING_PANELS_NO_STORYBOARD with 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_006/keyframes_16x9/, CIN006_keyframes_manifest_v1.json) + 18 s Ken Burns clip. NPC_HA_MAC / NPC_SAM_CHU_QUY have NO approved character lock: faces/costumes are storyboard placeholders, cinematic-only staging per DEC-MEDIA-P0 Q4. Known defects: S02 composition (oversized blurred glove + pale face-like shape at frame right) and cross-shot lighting drift, recorded per shot for the final-picture revision pass."
 ],
